        "The four-step transport model (generation, distribution, mode choice, assignment) embeds graph-theoretic shortest paths within a larger demand forecasting framework. User equilibrium assignment produces the realistic traffic loading that accounts for congestion effects — a more accurate but computationally demanding alternative to simple shortest-path routing.\n",
